/-!
# The actual scalar relative operators and their Haar coefficients

For an arbitrary holomorphic period family on an open subset of the
complex line, the genuine smooth torus-family operators `d0`, `d1`, and
`d2` are defined using actual base and vertical derivatives. Their literal
quotient lifts have the expected Fréchet derivative formulas. Their Haar
coefficients have exactly the base antiholomorphic derivative and the two
original marked relative symbols, including at frequency zero.
Vanishing of the base operator also satisfies the actual scalar
Cauchy--Riemann criterion.

This package supplies scalar differential operators, not cohomological
local generation, local freeness, or a higher-direct-image comparison.
-/
